Hokoreru jibun ga Toozakatteku

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.970
Your proud self will go far away

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.970
誇れる自分が 遠ざかってく

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:13.140
Mienai tsubasa de habataku no fly higher

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:13.140
Flapping the invisible wings to fly higher

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:13.140
見えない翼で羽ばたくの fly higher

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:20.470
Yume wo egaku no wa hito ni umareta kara

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:20.470
I'm imaging dreams because I was born a "person"

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:20.470
夢を描くのは「人」に生まれたから

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.580
Sora wo aogi Hoshi yo michite

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.580
Look up to the sky, rise to the stars,

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.580
空を仰ぎ 星よ満ちて

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.040
Tobitatsu no Asu e no brilliant road

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.040
Take-off on the brilliant road of tomorrow.

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.040
飛び立つの 明日への brilliant road

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.920
Kokoro no aosa Kono te ni daite

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.920
Carry the unexperienced of the heart in the hands

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.920
心の蒼さ この手に抱いて

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
Anata to nara Yowai jibun wo sarakedashite hashiridaseru no

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
If I were with you, I'd start running, exposing my weak self

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
あなたとなら 弱い自分をさらけ出して走り出せるの

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
Mirai yo dou ka Mugen ni tsuzuke go far away

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
The future! Somehow continues to the infinity, go far away

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
未来よどうか 無限に続け go far away

00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:06.020
Episode Thirteen:
 Winter Vacation

00:02:02.830 --> 00:02:04.920
This is FJ101, the Fujiyama.

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:07.600
We will be arriving at the Stellvia in five minutes.

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:09.450
We have finished confirmations as well.

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:10.640
Roger.

00:02:13.010 --> 00:02:17.730
Um... this goes here, and I'll put this in here...

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:19.960
And... after that...

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:23.100
What? That was creepy.

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:27.900
Somehow, you being so awkward makes you seem like a cute little girl.

00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:29.870
What do you mean by little girl?

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:33.740
That maybe you're still kind of a little kid.

00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:36.410
Well, why not?

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:37.610
It's not bad.

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:40.310
Shipon, you're so cute.

00:02:40.970 --> 00:02:42.940
Thank you, Arisa.

00:02:51.530 --> 00:02:53.410
I wonder where she is around now?

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:55.540
How many days does it take to get to the Ultima?

00:02:55.950 --> 00:02:56.790
40 days.

00:02:58.470 --> 00:03:00.520
This is no time to be sighing...

00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:03.040
...we have to hurry up and finish packing.

00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:04.640
I'm not packing.

00:03:04.970 --> 00:03:05.150
What?

00:03:05.810 --> 00:03:07.400
After all, I'm not going home.

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:09.950
What? Why? Why not?

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:13.820
Didn't I say? I'm not going home this time.

00:03:13.910 --> 00:03:16.480
What?!

00:03:16.830 --> 00:03:18.290
This is horrible, just horrible!

00:03:18.510 --> 00:03:21.600
In the first place, that's something you should have finished yesterday!

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:23.940
Well, you weren't packing, Arisa...

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:25.680
...so of course I was confused!

00:03:25.910 --> 00:03:28.600
And that's why I'm peddling so hard for you, right?!

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:30.440
Torya!

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:33.720
Banzai! Banzai!

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:36.170
Shima Katase, banzai!

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:40.080
Banzai! Banzai!

00:03:40.370 --> 00:03:42.600
Don't forget the souvenirs!

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:45.550
Aren't you going home?

00:03:45.810 --> 00:03:46.180
What?

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:51.040
No, there are some things going on with my family, so...

00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:57.750
Well, the Stellvia is open 24 hours a day, even at the end of the year...

00:03:58.070 --> 00:03:59.160
...so you won't get lonely.

00:04:21.050 --> 00:04:23.740
The gravity jump was executed without any problems.

00:04:24.260 --> 00:04:25.880
For the next three hours and 30 minutes...

00:04:26.350 --> 00:04:27.990
...please enjoy your trip through the sky.

00:04:34.390 --> 00:04:36.150
Shima-chan, let's go to the deck.

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:38.690
Hmm? Yeah, yeah, let's go.

00:04:41.590 --> 00:04:42.970
They're getting along rather well, aren't they?

00:04:43.120 --> 00:04:43.490
Huh?

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:45.170
Y-Yeah.

00:04:45.290 --> 00:04:46.530
H-Hi.

00:04:46.670 --> 00:04:47.280
Hi.

00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:49.340
Uh... See ya.

00:04:53.380 --> 00:04:54.400
See you later.

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:56.590
No, that's not it. Well...

00:04:57.130 --> 00:04:58.620
Jojo's a good guy, isn't he?

00:05:03.030 --> 00:05:06.330
This was green three months ago.

00:05:06.920 --> 00:05:09.170
And I hadn't met you, Shima-chan.

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:12.870
And I hadn't met you, either, Kouta.

00:05:16.450 --> 00:05:17.820
Maybe it IS kind of weird.

00:05:18.310 --> 00:05:21.460
My legs aren't pretty like Arisa's.

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:23.310
You're cute, Shima-chan.

00:05:27.880 --> 00:05:29.330
Um...

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:32.910
You know... it's that...

00:05:33.490 --> 00:05:36.210
When I look at you like this again, Kayama...

00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:38.520
This is kind of embarrassing.

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:42.690
But I'm really happy!

00:05:43.090 --> 00:05:45.260
Thank you. I am, too...

00:05:45.950 --> 00:05:48.760
You know, Shipon and Kouta were surprising...

00:05:49.110 --> 00:05:51.970
...but Jojo and Akira-chan were even more so.

00:05:56.710 --> 00:05:57.950
Oh, you going to hit on someone?

00:05:58.300 --> 00:05:59.880
Nothing as fickle as that.

00:06:00.530 --> 00:06:01.550
If I have to...

00:06:02.090 --> 00:06:04.150
Yeah, if I have to say this in one word, then I'd call it...

00:06:05.070 --> 00:06:05.590
...a challenge.

00:06:07.030 --> 00:06:07.640
Hi.

00:06:08.360 --> 00:06:09.230
Hi.

00:06:09.810 --> 00:06:10.300
Ahem.

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:11.800
What's wrong?

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:13.730
No, you see...

00:06:14.180 --> 00:06:16.430
I wanted to talk with you a bit, Milady...

00:06:17.420 --> 00:06:18.140
Would it be all right?

00:06:18.430 --> 00:06:19.290
Certainly.

00:06:22.590 --> 00:06:23.180
Thank you.

00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:29.990
Welcome to Nazca.

00:06:37.560 --> 00:06:42.140
In a moment, FJ101, the Fujiyama, will come into view.

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:41.060
<u>Current time</u>

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:41.060
<u>Departure Time </u>

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:41.060
<u>Estimated time of arrival</u>

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:41.060
<u>Flight time.</u>

00:06:41.060 --> 00:06:42.630
<u>Current time</u>

00:06:41.060 --> 00:06:42.630
<u>Ground speed </u>

00:06:41.060 --> 00:06:42.630
<u> External temperature </u>

00:06:41.060 --> 00:06:42.630
<u> Altitude</u>

00:06:42.690 --> 00:06:46.360
During landing, the video will look considerably unstable at times.

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:46.360
It's here! It's the Fujiyama!

00:06:46.740 --> 00:06:49.830
This is due to the influence of the gravity control.

00:06:50.670 --> 00:06:54.400
We assure you that the safety of the ship will not be compromised.

00:06:55.270 --> 00:06:57.240
We will be landing in just a moment.

00:06:57.310 --> 00:06:59.280
Our current speed is 20,000 meters.

00:07:06.720 --> 00:07:08.400
So, how did it go?

00:07:08.600 --> 00:07:10.590
Well... we talked quite a bit.

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:11.560
And?

00:07:11.870 --> 00:07:12.990
I died a warrior's death.

00:07:13.340 --> 00:07:15.430
I told her how I felt, and she turned me down with a smile.

00:07:15.940 --> 00:07:17.530
But you look so happy.

00:07:18.810 --> 00:07:19.670
Well, if I have to put it into words...

00:07:19.970 --> 00:07:22.800
...then I lost the battle, but won the war.

00:07:23.290 --> 00:07:24.700
What's that supposed to mean?

00:07:26.120 --> 00:07:28.170
Yayoi, what do you think of Pierre?

00:07:28.410 --> 00:07:29.160
What do you mean?

00:07:29.420 --> 00:07:31.150
Oh, I see...

00:07:31.500 --> 00:07:34.590
He seems pretty serious when he hits on you.

00:07:34.940 --> 00:07:35.810
That's true.

00:07:36.240 --> 00:07:37.630
If he tries a little harder...

00:07:37.690 --> 00:07:40.380
...Pierre might be able to find a wonderful girlfriend.

00:07:40.490 --> 00:07:41.040
What?
What?

00:07:41.620 --> 00:07:44.950
But I don't know whether or not it will be me.

00:07:45.260 --> 00:07:45.990
Huh?

00:07:46.420 --> 00:07:47.200
We're almost there.

00:08:08.620 --> 00:08:11.480
Wow, we're on the ground, we're on the ground!

00:08:11.720 --> 00:08:13.080
Katase.
Y-Yes?

00:08:13.490 --> 00:08:14.250
We need to talk to you.

00:08:14.700 --> 00:08:15.190
Yes?

00:08:16.290 --> 00:08:18.980
Where's Shima Katase? Where's Kouta Otoyama?

00:08:19.330 --> 00:08:20.290
Shima-chan!

00:08:22.340 --> 00:08:23.290
Shima There they are!

00:08:25.110 --> 00:08:26.170
It's Shima-chan!

00:08:26.170 --> 00:08:27.570
Kouta!

00:08:27.630 --> 00:08:29.880
W-Wait a second, this isn't what we agreed on!

00:08:30.230 --> 00:08:31.700
There are so many people!

00:08:47.410 --> 00:08:48.890
Is this really all right?

00:08:49.260 --> 00:08:51.860
You two are the heroes that saved the Earth and the surrounding area.

00:08:52.410 --> 00:08:53.920
Getting a personal transport is natural.

00:08:54.750 --> 00:08:57.160
I wonder if Akira and Jojo will be all right.

00:08:57.820 --> 00:08:59.840
They'll be fine once it's understood to be a case of mistaken identity.

00:09:00.220 --> 00:09:02.880
Of course, if it's not, then there's no guaranteeing their safety.

00:09:03.250 --> 00:09:05.050
Syoujin's there if anything happens.

00:09:06.810 --> 00:09:09.640
Bye, Shipon. See you next semester on the Stellvia.

00:09:09.950 --> 00:09:12.650
Though we might end up on the Fujiyama together before that.

00:09:13.080 --> 00:09:13.550
See you.

00:09:14.180 --> 00:09:15.210
Have a happy new year!

00:09:15.770 --> 00:09:16.310
Bye, then.

00:09:27.720 --> 00:09:30.550
Hey! Heya!

00:09:30.780 --> 00:09:32.810
Masato? Why?

00:09:33.350 --> 00:09:35.210
We got a notice from the Office of Space Development.

00:09:35.750 --> 00:09:37.870
You're quite the celebrity, coming in through the back way.

00:09:38.040 --> 00:09:38.880
Well, yeah.

00:09:40.290 --> 00:09:41.390
W-What?

00:09:41.830 --> 00:09:44.050
Big sister, you've gotten cuter, haven't you?

00:09:44.140 --> 00:09:45.620
W-What are you saying?

00:09:45.790 --> 00:09:49.290
Has the power of the stars changed the young girl, or could it be...

00:09:50.360 --> 00:09:50.880
Love?

00:09:57.090 --> 00:09:58.920
Thank you for always taking care of my big sister.

00:09:59.730 --> 00:10:00.890
I'm her younger brother, Masato.

00:10:01.550 --> 00:10:02.760
I'm Kouta Otoyama.

00:10:04.500 --> 00:10:05.970
Where are Dad and Mom?

00:10:06.150 --> 00:10:06.990
At work.

00:10:07.360 --> 00:10:10.140
There are lots of things to settle after the Second Wave, after all.

00:10:10.410 --> 00:10:13.170
More importantly, come this way.

00:10:14.420 --> 00:10:15.000
Hmm?
 Hmm?

00:10:20.340 --> 00:10:22.110
Shima-chan Otoyama still isn't here yet?

00:10:22.570 --> 00:10:23.920
This is strange.

00:10:24.940 --> 00:10:27.000
A lot of things... got damaged.

00:10:27.660 --> 00:10:29.540
But we had the shelters, after all.

00:10:29.990 --> 00:10:32.430
It feels like we escaped with the damage of an enormous typhoon.

00:10:33.880 --> 00:10:35.460
Thanks, you were a big help.

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:39.300
The two of you are the most famous people in Japan right now.

00:10:39.920 --> 00:10:41.450
You'll have to be careful from this point on.

00:10:41.740 --> 00:10:46.050
Speaking of which, if we're here, then will your family be all right?

00:10:46.660 --> 00:10:48.910
Aren't they coming to meet you at the lobby?

00:10:49.150 --> 00:10:50.560
No, they'll be fine.

00:10:51.110 --> 00:10:52.070
It looks like they've just arrived.

00:10:53.800 --> 00:10:54.540
What?
What?

00:11:03.290 --> 00:11:04.260
Wow!

00:11:04.820 --> 00:11:05.970
Gravity controls?

00:11:09.070 --> 00:11:09.800
Hi!

00:11:10.250 --> 00:11:10.600
What?

00:11:11.120 --> 00:11:12.130
That's my older sister, Youko.

00:11:12.570 --> 00:11:13.060
What?!

00:11:16.540 --> 00:11:17.340
Nice to meet you.

00:11:35.960 --> 00:11:37.120
Whoa!

00:11:37.190 --> 00:11:39.950
This is amazing! This is amazing!

00:11:40.440 --> 00:11:42.730
Yeah... yeah... I'm fine.

00:11:43.360 --> 00:11:47.040
All right, then tell Chi-chan I said hi.

00:11:47.590 --> 00:11:48.370
How was it?

00:11:48.870 --> 00:11:51.490
It's all right. He said to go and have fun.

00:11:51.810 --> 00:11:53.660
That's right, you should enjoy yourself.

00:11:54.180 --> 00:11:55.910
You live in Kamakura, right, Shima-chan?

00:11:56.550 --> 00:11:59.470
Afterwards, I can use this to give you a lift straight to your house.

00:11:59.930 --> 00:12:00.910
Thank you.

00:12:01.090 --> 00:12:04.160
That way is faster, so it's a big help.
Hey, now.

00:12:04.300 --> 00:12:08.450
But you know, today it took four hours to get from Kamakura to Tokyo.

00:12:08.840 --> 00:12:10.520
And two hours to get to the airport.

00:12:10.860 --> 00:12:12.550
It took six hours?

00:12:12.830 --> 00:12:14.650
Then when did you wake up, Masato?

00:12:14.730 --> 00:12:15.700
4:00 in the morning.

00:12:15.920 --> 00:12:19.540
But it was all for the sake of my cute elder sister.

00:12:19.630 --> 00:12:20.160
Dummy.

00:12:20.640 --> 00:12:24.630
That's right, a pretty older sister really is nice to have, isn't it?

00:12:24.690 --> 00:12:25.120
Yes.

00:12:25.640 --> 00:12:28.420
Though your prettiness is a much better prettiness.

00:12:29.810 --> 00:12:30.970
Oh, you're the greatest.

00:12:34.030 --> 00:12:35.440
No matter what they say...

00:12:35.750 --> 00:12:38.250
...the Second Wave's effect was huge.

00:12:48.280 --> 00:12:49.000
Yeah...

00:12:51.030 --> 00:12:53.460
What? Shima-chan's not coming home?

00:12:53.780 --> 00:12:54.900
No, no...

00:12:55.280 --> 00:12:57.300
She's stopping by a friend's house first, then coming home.

00:12:57.850 --> 00:13:00.050
Then is she staying there tonight?

00:13:00.430 --> 00:13:02.340
No, she said she'll be home by evening.

00:13:02.940 --> 00:13:06.240
It looks like that family has a gravity vehicle.

00:13:06.270 --> 00:13:07.020
Yeah...?

00:13:07.400 --> 00:13:10.430
Oh, then I'd better get things ready for tonight's dinner.

00:13:10.430 --> 00:13:10.870
What?

00:13:11.290 --> 00:13:12.650
What in the world does that mean?

00:13:13.270 --> 00:13:16.160
I was certain that Shima-chan wouldn't be arriving until nighttime...

00:13:16.320 --> 00:13:17.630
...so she'd be eating out somewhere.

00:13:18.120 --> 00:13:20.810
But if she's going to make it by evening time, then a feast...

00:13:21.160 --> 00:13:23.290
We have to make a feast and wait for her!

00:13:23.560 --> 00:13:24.430
I understand.

00:13:24.980 --> 00:13:25.930
Then I'll...

00:13:26.020 --> 00:13:27.060
I'm going to make it!

00:13:27.440 --> 00:13:30.040
What? But will you be all right?

00:13:30.300 --> 00:13:31.170
I will!

00:13:31.400 --> 00:13:33.390
If I finish up my work at mach speed...

00:13:33.510 --> 00:13:35.650
...leave work early and shop as I go home...

00:13:35.990 --> 00:13:38.080
...I'll be able to pull it off. It's all right!

00:13:38.130 --> 00:13:39.450
Hey, now.

00:13:40.770 --> 00:13:41.520
All right!

00:13:54.820 --> 00:13:55.320
That's it.

00:13:55.570 --> 00:13:56.620
Wow!

00:14:16.100 --> 00:14:19.690
Wow, that's incredible! It looks just like a secret base!

00:14:44.350 --> 00:14:46.880
Is this really just your house here, Kouta?

00:14:47.070 --> 00:14:50.480
Yeah. Apparently no one lived here before us.

00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:52.150
I guess my father and mother moved here...

00:14:52.220 --> 00:14:54.450
...because you can see the stars really well.

00:14:55.990 --> 00:14:57.340
What's with that astronomical observatory?

00:14:58.000 --> 00:14:59.220
My father made it.

00:14:59.820 --> 00:15:01.930
Right now, my sister is the second chief.

00:15:02.660 --> 00:15:03.500
Are you okay with not going?

00:15:04.900 --> 00:15:06.790
It would have been okay to go with them.

00:15:07.230 --> 00:15:08.590
I would have been intruding.

00:15:11.360 --> 00:15:13.360
You really are levelheaded, aren't you?

00:15:13.740 --> 00:15:15.640
My big sister was kind of flighty...

00:15:16.040 --> 00:15:19.080
...so I guess because of that, I ended up being levelheaded.

00:15:19.430 --> 00:15:21.140
My mother is kind of careless, and my father is carefree...

00:15:21.620 --> 00:15:23.850
...and I guess you could say that he goes at his own pace...

00:15:24.350 --> 00:15:26.660
So at the very least, I had to be a stand-up person.

00:15:27.180 --> 00:15:27.930
I see.

00:15:28.420 --> 00:15:31.660
Our father and mother died very early on.

00:15:32.380 --> 00:15:34.820
I was 17, and Kouta was four when they died...

00:15:35.220 --> 00:15:35.730
Huh.

00:15:36.430 --> 00:15:39.300
For a while, our uncle supported us...

00:15:39.840 --> 00:15:41.610
...but when I turned 20, I came back here.

00:15:41.900 --> 00:15:42.770
To this island?

00:15:42.970 --> 00:15:43.400
Mm-hmm.

00:15:44.990 --> 00:15:47.620
But I wonder if it was right to bring Kouta here or not...

00:15:48.350 --> 00:15:51.320
As you can see, he has an unusual air about him, right?

00:15:52.980 --> 00:15:54.470
It's so hard to raise a child.

00:15:54.770 --> 00:15:59.480
Let's see... this means that you would be about 30...

00:15:59.650 --> 00:16:01.210
Hey, now! That's not it, right?

00:16:01.100 --> 00:16:04.100
Incoming Call

00:16:04.100 --> 00:16:07.110
Incoming Call

00:16:09.510 --> 00:16:10.860
Wow...

00:16:12.400 --> 00:16:14.870
If we had time, we could go in the ocean.

00:16:15.010 --> 00:16:17.530
I see. I bet it's beautiful.

00:16:18.940 --> 00:16:20.730
Your sister is someone who looks at the stars?

00:16:21.050 --> 00:16:23.310
She's effectively the second chief here.

00:16:23.710 --> 00:16:25.620
Who does this place belong to?

00:16:26.140 --> 00:16:28.610
The Office of Space Development? The Sol System Alliance?

00:16:29.290 --> 00:16:32.500
Apparently, there's support from the Alliance and other places...

00:16:32.910 --> 00:16:35.190
...but this place doesn't seem to belong to anyone.

00:16:35.280 --> 00:16:36.720
Hmm... Oh!

00:16:37.300 --> 00:16:39.240
The Otoyama Astronomical Research Center?

00:16:39.500 --> 00:16:40.220
Close.

00:16:40.690 --> 00:16:42.620
The Astronomy Island Otoyama Astronomical Center.

00:16:42.970 --> 00:16:44.530
That's not close at all.

00:16:46.120 --> 00:16:46.870
Well, that's true.

00:16:59.110 --> 00:17:01.220
I'm sorry, but we'll be there soon.

00:17:01.850 --> 00:17:03.380
Okay. I'm all right.

00:17:10.700 --> 00:17:12.120
It's huge!

00:17:24.260 --> 00:17:25.710
Wow!

00:17:42.020 --> 00:17:45.290
I'd like to come for a proper visit next time.

00:17:59.630 --> 00:18:03.440
I want to go to the Stellvia, too. Follow my sister, and surpass her.

00:18:03.970 --> 00:18:06.890
You respect your sister, don't you, Masato?

00:18:07.060 --> 00:18:08.010
Yes, I do.

00:18:08.620 --> 00:18:10.250
I may say a lot of things...

00:18:11.050 --> 00:18:12.810
But my sister is my idol.

00:18:16.860 --> 00:18:18.820
Seven Incoming Calls

00:18:17.150 --> 00:18:17.760
What the...?

00:18:17.900 --> 00:18:18.620
What's wrong?

00:18:19.290 --> 00:18:22.390
My cell phone... it looks like there were a lot of incoming calls.

00:18:22.760 --> 00:18:24.240
I had turned it off, so...

00:18:26.900 --> 00:18:27.630
Mine's the same.

00:18:28.050 --> 00:18:30.110
From the Tokyo branch of the Office of Space Development...

00:18:30.300 --> 00:18:32.160
I wonder what it could be?
Yeah...

00:18:33.400 --> 00:18:35.840
Oh, there's no time!

00:18:36.060 --> 00:18:40.370
If I broil this while I ladle those... um... um...

00:18:40.490 --> 00:18:42.980
Hey, Umihito, how am I supposed to do this?

00:18:43.150 --> 00:18:45.230
You don't have to rush so much.

00:18:45.580 --> 00:18:46.920
You'll still make it.

00:18:46.990 --> 00:18:48.500
But that will cause a huge accident!

00:18:51.590 --> 00:18:53.470
That is what will cause a huge accident.

00:18:54.140 --> 00:18:54.510
Huh?

00:18:55.070 --> 00:18:55.790
Incoming

00:18:55.070 --> 00:18:55.320
Call With Video

00:18:56.650 --> 00:18:57.260
Yes?

00:18:57.350 --> 00:18:59.290
Are you the parent of Shima Katase?

00:18:59.890 --> 00:19:02.150
Yes. Are you with the Office of Space Development?

00:19:02.610 --> 00:19:05.410
Yes, I'm Yasuike with the Tokyo branch.

00:19:07.060 --> 00:19:09.170
Okay then, Kouta, ma'am!

00:19:09.290 --> 00:19:10.800
Thank you very much.

00:19:11.460 --> 00:19:13.190
Okay, then. Have a happy new year.

00:19:13.600 --> 00:19:15.850
My younger brother is kind of complicated...

00:19:16.200 --> 00:19:17.070
...so please take care of him.

00:19:17.210 --> 00:19:18.020
What's with that?

00:19:20.510 --> 00:19:21.060
Bye, then!

00:19:23.400 --> 00:19:27.220
Maybe we should introduce ourselves to her parents, too.

00:19:27.450 --> 00:19:29.880
What? What are you saying, big sister?

00:19:33.290 --> 00:19:35.020
Hello, this is Otoyama...

00:19:38.730 --> 00:19:39.600
What's wrong?

00:19:40.000 --> 00:19:43.060
Nothing... Chi-chan... Mom...

00:19:43.180 --> 00:19:45.670
What would be good for me to say to her?

00:19:45.930 --> 00:19:48.270
What in the world are you talking about?

00:19:48.590 --> 00:19:50.610
Big sister, you're her daughter, so it's all right.

00:19:50.960 --> 00:19:52.230
Just say, "I'm home," as always.

00:19:53.100 --> 00:19:55.080
But it's been so long...

00:19:55.270 --> 00:19:58.210
You did something SO bold, so it'll be all right.

00:19:59.890 --> 00:20:00.350
Huh?

00:20:01.050 --> 00:20:04.060
Y-Y-You saw that? W-What?

00:20:06.430 --> 00:20:08.250
Huh? What's wrong?

00:20:08.570 --> 00:20:10.300
I'm talking about the Great Mission.

00:20:12.990 --> 00:20:16.900
Or did something else bold happen, dear sister?

00:20:19.900 --> 00:20:21.410
Masato!

00:20:27.220 --> 00:20:28.110
Special News Report This is a special news report.

00:20:28.840 --> 00:20:31.350
Today, Foundation Six, the Ultima...

00:20:31.670 --> 00:20:35.200
...has entered a state of battle with unknown flying objects.

00:20:35.490 --> 00:20:39.620
It's been 60 years since a case of live rounds being used in an act of force.

00:20:39.880 --> 00:20:43.410
The details are as yet unknown. Things are still being investigated.

00:20:44.020 --> 00:20:45.780
An emergency assembly?

00:20:46.190 --> 00:20:47.920
It was a request from the Office of Space Development.

00:20:48.440 --> 00:20:50.700
They asked for you to go back as soon as you can.

00:20:50.930 --> 00:20:51.700
Right now?!

00:20:52.120 --> 00:20:52.930
Big sister...

00:21:10.710 --> 00:21:12.890
This is Yasuike. They just took off.

00:21:13.310 --> 00:21:15.280
As soon as they arrive, the Fujiyama will head to the Stellvia.

00:21:20.770 --> 00:21:24.560
It'll be all right. It's not like they're going off to fight.

00:21:24.620 --> 00:21:25.370
Right...

00:21:35.490 --> 00:21:36.420
Mom...

00:21:55.960 --> 00:22:01.050
kono sora no iku hate ni

00:21:55.960 --> 00:22:01.050
Where the end of this sky goes

00:21:55.960 --> 00:22:01.050
この空の行く果てに

00:22:04.520 --> 00:22:10.970
mada mienu mirai no nami ga ri

00:22:04.520 --> 00:22:10.970
Are waves of the future that cannot yet be seen

00:22:04.520 --> 00:22:10.970
まだ見えぬ 未来の波があり

00:22:12.190 --> 00:22:21.010
ikite iru ikutsu mono unmei o koete yuku

00:22:12.190 --> 00:22:21.010
We are alive; we overcome many destinies

00:22:12.190 --> 00:22:21.010
生きている いくつもの運命を越えて行く

00:22:21.440 --> 00:22:28.780
dare ni osowari dare ni koute iru no darou

00:22:21.440 --> 00:22:28.780
Who are we learning from, who are we asking?

00:22:21.440 --> 00:22:28.780
誰に教わり 誰に請うているのだろう

00:22:29.100 --> 00:22:37.600
hito wa tsukiru inochi no aima ni

00:22:29.100 --> 00:22:37.600
People do not have time to fear encountering

00:22:29.100 --> 00:22:37.600
人は尽きる命の合間に

00:22:37.890 --> 00:22:46.570
deau koto ni obieru ma wa nai

00:22:37.890 --> 00:22:46.570
The space between expiring lives

00:22:37.890 --> 00:22:46.570
出会うことに 怯える間はない

00:22:46.570 --> 00:22:57.240
tatoe kyou de kono sekai ga owarou to shite ite mo

00:22:46.570 --> 00:22:57.240
Even if this world would end today

00:22:46.570 --> 00:22:57.240
たとえ今日で この世界が終わろうとしていても

00:22:57.410 --> 00:23:02.820
kimi o ai suru darou

00:22:57.410 --> 00:23:02.820
I will still love you

00:22:57.410 --> 00:23:02.820
君を愛するだろう

00:23:05.020 --> 00:23:06.980
Next Episode

00:23:06.720 --> 00:23:07.530
This is Shima.

00:23:07.480 --> 00:23:08.510
This is Arisa!

00:23:08.580 --> 00:23:10.540
I wonder why there's an emergency assembly?

00:23:10.520 --> 00:23:11.490
I wonder why.

00:23:11.580 --> 00:23:13.580
It's probably just a sudden callback. It'll be all right.

00:23:13.650 --> 00:23:17.220
But for some reason, there's a heavy mood to it...

00:23:17.290 --> 00:23:20.890
"Emergency Assembly" sounds scary.

00:23:20.980 --> 00:23:22.680
Really? In that case, how about saying it like this:

00:23:22.800 --> 00:23:24.530
"Emergency Assembly!"

00:23:24.600 --> 00:23:26.290
That seems kind of stupid.

00:23:26.760 --> 00:23:28.380
Hi shu shan shun shou!

00:23:28.860 --> 00:23:30.530
On the next episode of Stellvia of the Universe...

00:23:30.600 --> 00:23:31.590
"Dream and Reality."

00:23:31.670 --> 00:23:32.480
Please look forward to it!

00:23:32.050 --> 00:23:35.050
Episode 14 
Dream and Reality 

00:23:32.670 --> 00:23:34.800
Dream and Reality Is this a dream? Or reality?
